## Description

The `toJSON()` method is automatically called by JSON.stringify() when a `Temporal.PlainDateTime` object is stringified. This method is generally intended to, by default, usefully serialize `Temporal.PlainDateTime` objects during [JSON](/en-US/docs/Glossary/JSON) serialization, which can then be deserialized using the {{jsxref("Temporal/PlainDateTime/from", "Temporal.PlainDateTime.from()")}} function within the reviver of JSON.parse().

## Examples

### Using toJSON()

```js
const dt = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from({ year: 2021, month: 8, day: 1 });
const dtStr = dt.toJSON(); // '2021-08-01T00:00:00'
