```js-nolint
keys()
```

### Parameters

None.

### Return value

A new [iterable iterator object](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Iterator).

## Examples

### Using keys()

```js
const myMap = new Map();
myMap.set("0", "foo");
myMap.set(1, "bar");
myMap.set({}, "baz");

const mapIter = myMap.keys();

console.log(mapIter.next().value); // "0"
console.log(mapIter.next().value); // 1
